MAJOR_VERSION=4
STANDARD_VERSION=0
RELEASE_VERSION=1
PRERELEASE=1
DEV_VERSION=1
DESCRIPTION<<VER_4_0_1_COMBINED
Makefile: top-level builds default to -j1 (serial compile jobs) unless the user passes an explicit job count (-j/--jobs) or inherits a parallel jobserver; reduces out-of-memory kills from gcc on low-RAM hosts while keeping parallel builds one flag away.

Also includes host IPC and shell/PIC hardening merged from a sibling agent branch: pipe_write returns -1 with EAGAIN when the ring cannot accept a non-zero write; msgq_send sets errno (EINVAL, EPIPE, EAGAIN); msgq_create rejects max_messages*message_size overflow and checks pthread init failures; pipe_create checks pthread init failures; VM popup path NUL-terminates exe_path after strncpy; bare-metal 8259 PIC EOI skips spurious IRQ7 and IRQ15; fl/ipc.h documents return/errno behavior; userspace connection tests extended (pipe/msgq EAGAIN, wrong-handle rejects, msgq recv errno paths, size overflow on msgq_create).

cd: NUL-terminate g_cwd when getcwd fails after chdir. Shell: check pthread mutex/cond init and pthread_create; guard batch command totalLen against size_t overflow; pthread_create failure path signals shutdown under g_pool.mutex before join; register atexit(shell_pool_cleanup) so exit() paths join workers and destroy pool primitives; batch setdisk/createdisk accepts cmd plus three args (four tokens) and consumes an optional fifth -y/-n flag; too-few-arg paths consume dangling argv tokens instead of re-dispatching them as commands. IPC: msgq_receive sets errno (EINVAL, EPIPE, EAGAIN, ETIMEDOUT) on host; timed-wait returns ETIMEDOUT only when the queue is still empty after pthread_cond_timedwait (avoids false timeout if a message arrived at the deadline edge); pipe_write documents TODO to keep pre-lock checks minimal. VFS: safer size_t bounds for legacy disk ruler/allocs, cluster table malloc, format path; update_cluster_line checks strdup and uses size_t-safe hex line length; fs import_text_drive uses per-call heap line table (thread-safe) plus import ruler/zeros; remove_directory_recursive hoists directory scan helpers to file scope (standard C); FAT32 bytes-per-cluster multiply overflow guard; fat32_host_load rejects root_cluster<2 before cluster math; fat32_host_format_image guards FLINT.DAT size in directory entry and frees rootbuf/closes fd on that overflow; fat32_host_files cluster-chain length computed in uint64_t before cast (SIZE_MAX/UINT32_MAX checks); import_text_drive fails fast on zero-buffer OOM or cluster-size overflow instead of silently skipping cluster lines; FAT chain iteration guards use uint64_t caps (no uint32_t wrap); free_cluster_chain bounded against cycles; allocate_and_write_chain rollback clears the partially linked cluster; max_cluster_number clamps UINT32_MAX+1 wrap; Makefile drops duplicate %.o:%.s rule and treats --jobserver-auth as an active jobserver for default -j1.
VER_4_0_1_COMBINED

RELEASE_DATE=2026-05-18
